      "body": "Design record for #5881 (task 14333), following the sibling #5874/#5876 pattern under parent #5683: `doc/2026-11-10_design_id5881_stepup_escrow.md`, indexed in doc/README.md.\n\nSettles, within the parent framework's givens (opt-in capabilities only; §6.3 step-up shape; §6.4 escrow/assertion/audit shape; configured consent or no proxy use):\n- D1 step-up gates: declaration-listed event class + required factor class + window scoped per (subject, server, event class); IdP performs the factor, the server consumes a signed step-up assertion.\n- D2 escrow contents: org-issued material, evidence originals, recovery shares — never the sole copy of a user credential, never user passwords or raw biometrics.\n- D3 proxied assertions: signed, recipient-bound, short-lived, minimal claim kinds; raw-value proxying only as the consented, stepped-up exception.\n- D4 consent: standing per-kind default, per-use for raw reveals. **Flagged scoping decision:** org-authority alone never authorizes proxying user-owned material — recorded explicitly here and on #5881 per the acceptance, narrowing the parent §11 menu for user-owned material only.\n- D5 audit (parent field set + step-up fields, no raw values), D6 user visibility as an unremovable floor incl. revocation, D7 fail-closed gated actions with break-glass as the only bypass.\n- Invariants, rejected alternatives, and two open points routed back to #5683.\n\nDocs-only. Closes #5881\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796940487&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8321&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8321&signature=ff67c2cce7488a650c26a3e061ca32473a03474609ae5c63801ac5f541edcf67\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-co