      "body": "Implements #7783 — step 1 of the #5683 evidence assurance layer (design `doc/2026-11-08_design_id5683.md` §3/§9, in PR #7781).\n\n## What\n\nAdditive only, all in `pkgs/id/crates/id-core/src/residency.rs` (+335 lines, no existing line changed):\n\n- **`AssuranceLevel`** — ordered `SelfDeclared` (the design's `Self`, L0) < `OrgAttested` (L1) < `ProviderVerified` (L2). Stored, never inferred; nothing auto-promotes (#5876 §2).\n- **`PrivacyClass`** — `Exact` / `Derived` / `VerdictOnly` (§3.3).\n- **`SubjectEvidence`** — the §3.1 envelope: `subject`, `assurance`, `basis` (provenance reference, never raw documents), `privacy_class`, and the **unchanged** placement `Evidence`. Per §3.1/§9 the public shape of `Evidence` does not change.\n- **`Declaration`** — scope + subject + `min_assurance` (the §2.3 `evidence_req` bar, reduced to step 1).\n- **`evaluate_declared()`** — the thin pre-step: filters claims to the declared subject, checks the assurance bar, maps surviving claims to the `Hop`s `evaluate()` consumes, and delegates placement to `evaluate()` unchanged. No second evaluator.\n- **`AssuredDecision` / `AssuranceDenyReason`** — assurance-bar rejection is a typed reason (`BelowAssuranceBar { plane, required, offered }`, `NoSubjectEvidence(Plane)`) distinguishable from every existing `DenyReason` variant, as the acceptance criteria require.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [x] Assurance bar rejection produces a typed reason distinguishable from the existing `DenyReason` variants.\n- [x] Property test: `property_below_bar_never_allows` — exhaustive over every (offered, required) level pair and every single below-bar plane; oracle: below-bar evidence never yields `Allow`.\n- [x] Existing `residency.rs` tests pass unchanged (no existing test or line modified).\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test -p id-core --lib residency` on the laptop: **24 passed, 0 failed** (18 pre-existing + 6 new assurance tests). The 4 build warnings are pre-existing (`access.rs`, `world_caps.rs`, and the pre-existing `Decision` missing-docs note).\n\nQueue: task 14558, lane code-n.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796931656&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8197&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8197&signature=e5c74a705c127e8f2b7e11353f0575c9169f3cdcbdcc5284be34c89a503611eb\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8197?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
